//// Decision 676 (2) — "most dependencies last" is the deepest chain, not
//// the count: `wide` depends on three packages, one level down; `deep`
//// depends on `mid`, which depends on `base`, two levels down. `deep`'s
//// executors run last, after `wide`'s, though `wide` has more
//// dependencies; `mid` runs after `wide`, both one level up, in the
//// depth-first order the manifests give.

